<title>USA: Natural gas storage levels drawn down in Texas.</title>
<headline>Natural gas storage levels drawn down in Texas.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natural gas in storage in Texas fell to 137.3 billion cubic feet (bcf) in January, down from 181.8 bcf in December and 232.6 bcf in December 1995, the Texas Railroad Commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>The commission, which regulates oil and natural gas production in the state, trimmed allowable production from prorated fields in the state to 64.8 bcf during February compared to 72.4 bcf in February 1996.</p>
</text>
